# dependencies and build output
node_modules/
vscode-extension/out/
*.vsix
# C2: `vscode-extension/core/mlview` is the analyzer the VSIX SHIPS, and it is a
# BUILT artifact, not a source of truth. `tools/sync-core.py` writes it, `npm run
# compile`, `npm run package` (through `vscode:prepublish`) and `scripts/build.*`
# all run that first, and `tools/verify.py --vsix` checks the built copy against
# `analyzer/src/mlview`.
# One analyzer is tracked in this repository (`analyzer/src/mlview`) plus one
# vendored copy that a marketplace install of the Claude Code plugin needs
# verbatim (`claude-plugin/vendor/mlview`, which goes away once the wheel is on
# PyPI). A third tracked copy only ever added ~120 files of review surface.
vscode-extension/core/
# PACKAGING: `python -m build --wheel analyzer` (scripts/build.sh step 6) writes both.
analyzer/dist/
analyzer/build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# PUB-01: `python tools/public_corpus.py fetch` clones ~1.8 GB of pinned public
# repositories into tools/public_corpus.py's DEFAULT_CORPUS_DIR (override it with
# MLVIEW_PUBLIC_CORPUS_DIR). The manifest pins every SHA, so the clones are
# reproducible from analyzer/tests/public_corpus/repos.json and are never
# committed. Without this line a developer who runs `fetch` gets 37 untracked
# repositories in `git status`, and the module docstring's "git-ignored" is false.
.public-corpus/

# `python -m mlview init` writes `<root>/.mlview.toml` (CONTRACTS D1), and running
# the tool on its OWN checkout - a demo, an e2e pass, the VS Code "Open MLView
# Configuration" command - lands one here. Every key in it is commented out, so
# it configures nothing; it is a generated artifact, not this repository's
# config. Only the leading slash is ignored, so a `.mlview.toml` a USER commits
# in their own project is untouched, and `git add -f .mlview.toml` still works
# the day MLView decides to dogfood a real one.
/.mlview.toml

# generated demo artifacts (scripts/e2e regenerates them)
.mlview/
webview/.mlview/
# MLV-P11: `python analyzer/tools/gen_gallery.py` renders ~90 self-contained reports
# (~30 MB) from the rule fixtures and the clean corpus. Zero new content, so it is
# generated on demand and never committed.
docs/gallery/

# local orchestration backups and scratch
# C5: `.workflows/` held the multi-agent orchestration scripts of past sprints —
# session artifacts full of absolute machine paths, not part of the product.
.workflows/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local virtual environment (macOS setup)
.venv/

# editor and OS scratch that no checkout should carry
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# coverage output (`pytest --cov`, `c8`/`nyc`); no gate reads a committed report
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
